{"id": "D017", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "The emergency change must be reviewed retrospectively at CAB within 2 working days of implementation. The post-incident review meeting must take place within 5 working days of the service being restored.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["OPS-102:v2.0:s5:c1", "OPS-101:v3.0:s7:c1"], "cited_text": {"OPS-102:v2.0:s5:c1": "An emergency change can be approved by the Duty Operations Manager and the system owner together. Approval can be given by phone but must be recorded in the ticket. Every emergency change must be reviewed retrospectively at CAB within 2 working days of implementation.", "OPS-101:v3.0:s7:c1": "Every P1 incident needs a post-incident review. The review meeting must take place within 5 working days of the service being restored. The system owner writes the review, which records the timeline, the root cause, what went well and the actions agreed, each with an owner and a due date. Reviews are stored with the incident ticket."}, "cited_by_model": ["OPS-102:v2.0:s5:c1", "OPS-101:v3.0:s7:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "OPS-101:v3.0:s7:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.6779100894927979, "sections": ["OPS-101#7"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s5:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.617965579032898, "sections": ["OPS-102#5"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s2:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.5515492558479309, "sections": ["OPS-102#2"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s4:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.5324841737747192, "sections": ["OPS-102#4"]}, {"id": "OPS-101:v3.0:s5:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.5136662125587463, "sections": ["OPS-101#5"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 1024, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 87, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "embedding_tokens": 30, "cost_usd": 0.00014649999999999998, "retrieval_ms": 161.66489999977784, "generation_ms": 1697.161099999903, "total_ms": 1858.8259999996808, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_a10e70e450bd47b19f033a5060d4807d", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D018", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "A business trip abroad needs a director’s approval before booking. You may work remotely from abroad for up to 10 working days per calendar year, with your line manager’s approval.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["HR-202:v2.0:s6:c1", "HR-203:v1.3:s5:c1"], "cited_text": {"HR-202:v2.0:s6:c1": "Trips outside the UK need approval from a director before booking. Check the travel advice for the destination and tell the Service Desk before you travel so that your laptop and phone will work abroad.", "HR-203:v1.3:s5:c1": "You may work from outside the UK for up to 10 working days in a calendar year with approval from your line manager. Ask the Service Desk to check your laptop before you go. Working abroad for longer is not allowed, because of tax and employment law."}, "cited_by_model": ["HR-202:v2.0:s6:c1", "HR-203:v1.3:s5:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s5:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.7100491523742676, "sections": ["HR-203#5"]}, {"id": "HR-202:v2.0:s6:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.6303837895393372, "sections": ["HR-202#6"]}, {"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s3:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.47577014565467834, "sections": ["HR-203#3"]}, {"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s2:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.45430341362953186, "sections": ["HR-203#2"]}, {"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s5:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.4468362331390381, "sections": ["HR-201#5"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 897, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 124, "reasoning_tokens": 37, "embedding_tokens": 26, "cost_usd": 0.00015222, "retrieval_ms": 175.85150000013527, "generation_ms": 1967.8213999995933, "total_ms": 2143.6728999997285, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_8eb14a7c8c49435692b3b339c4112064", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D019", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "Accident book entries are kept for 3 years from the date of the entry. For contractors working at height, the site manager issues the permit to work.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["SEC-302:v3.1:s3:c1", "FAC-401:v2.0:s2:c1"], "cited_text": {"SEC-302:v3.1:s3:c1": "| Record | Retention period |\n|---|---|\n| Payroll records | 6 years after the end of the tax year they relate to |\n| Personnel files for leavers | 6 years after the leaving date |\n| Applications from unsuccessful candidates | 6 months after the recruitment decision |\n| Accident book entries | 3 years from the date of the entry |", "FAC-401:v2.0:s2:c1": "Contractors must complete the site safety induction before starting work. The induction is valid for 12 months at the site where it was completed. Contractors carrying out hot work, work at height or work on electrical systems need a permit to work issued by the site manager."}, "cited_by_model": ["SEC-302:v3.1:s3:c1", "FAC-401:v2.0:s2:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "FAC-401:v2.0:s2:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.5437910556793213, "sections": ["FAC-401#2"]}, {"id": "SEC-302:v3.1:s3:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.477583646774292, "sections": ["SEC-302#3"]}, {"id": "FAC-401:v2.0:s5:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.45540785789489746, "sections": ["FAC-401#5"]}, {"id": "SEC-302:v3.1:s2:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.43337199091911316, "sections": ["SEC-302#2"]}, {"id": "FAC-401:v2.0:s1:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.4076812267303467, "sections": ["FAC-401#1"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 971, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 108, "reasoning_tokens": 25, "embedding_tokens": 21, "cost_usd": 0.00015152, "retrieval_ms": 154.31189999981143, "generation_ms": 1553.4336000000621, "total_ms": 1707.7454999998736, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_1b952143ea954811b21a5cbfa4bbb0ec", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D020", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "The manager must order the laptop at least 10 working days before the start date. Request system access through the service portal using the “System access” form.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["OPS-105:v1.1:s2:c1", "OPS-104:v2.2:s2:c1"], "cited_text": {"OPS-105:v1.1:s2:c1": "New starters receive their laptop and phone from the Service Desk on their first day. The line manager must order equipment at least 10 working days before the start date. Each item is recorded against the person's name with its asset tag.", "OPS-104:v2.2:s2:c1": "Request access through the service portal using the \"System access\" form. Requests are fulfilled within 2 working days of the final approval. Do not share your login with a colleague who is waiting for access."}, "cited_by_model": ["OPS-105:v1.1:s2:c1", "OPS-104:v2.2:s2:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "OPS-105:v1.1:s2:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.6555689573287964, "sections": ["OPS-105#2"]}, {"id": "OPS-104:v2.2:s3:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.47033587098121643, "sections": ["OPS-104#3"]}, {"id": "OPS-104:v2.2:s2:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.45415249466896057, "sections": ["OPS-104#2"]}, {"id": "OPS-105:v1.1:s5:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.439144492149353, "sections": ["OPS-105#5"]}, {"id": "OPS-104:v2.2:s5:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.4351520538330078, "sections": ["OPS-104#5"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 976, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 128, "reasoning_tokens": 45, "embedding_tokens": 27, "cost_usd": 0.00016214000000000002, "retrieval_ms": 160.0402000003669, "generation_ms": 1897.483700000521, "total_ms": 2057.523900000888, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_20bb4892893f41ea80df697ade697a98", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D021", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "No. Claims must be submitted within 60 days of the date the cost was incurred; later claims will not be paid unless the Finance Director agrees there were exceptional circumstances.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["HR-201:v4.0:s2:c1"], "cited_text": {"HR-201:v4.0:s2:c1": "Submit claims through the expenses system within 60 days of the date the cost was incurred. Claims submitted later will not be paid unless the Finance Director agrees there were exceptional circumstances. Claims are paid with the next monthly payroll after approval."}, "cited_by_model": ["HR-201:v4.0:s2:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s2:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.7125815749168396, "sections": ["HR-201#2"]}, {"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s6:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.512148916721344, "sections": ["HR-201#6"]}, {"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s3:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.46092212200164795, "sections": ["HR-201#3"]}, {"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s5:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.44884926080703735, "sections": ["HR-201#5"]}, {"id": "HR-201:v4.0:s1:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.4434140920639038, "sections": ["HR-201#1"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 873, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 106, "reasoning_tokens": 33, "embedding_tokens": 18, "cost_usd": 0.00014066000000000003, "retrieval_ms": 191.0450999994282, "generation_ms": 1937.9580000004353, "total_ms": 2129.0030999998635, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_c64634f9980e40408cc487e4711fc328", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D022", "status": "ok", "outcome": "conflicting_evidence", "answer": "The handbook passages give different replacement cycles: the hybrid-working policy says every 3 years, while the IT equipment policy says every 4 years.", "conflict_note": "HR-203 specifies a 3-year cycle for hybrid workers’ laptops; OPS-105 specifies a 4-year cycle for laptops.", "citations": ["HR-203:v1.3:s6:c1", "OPS-105:v1.1:s6:c1"], "cited_text": {"HR-203:v1.3:s6:c1": "The company provides a laptop, a monitor and a headset for hybrid workers. Laptops for hybrid workers are replaced every 3 years. If you leave Fernhollow, return all company equipment, including your laptop, within 10 working days of your last working day.", "OPS-105:v1.1:s6:c1": "Laptops are replaced every 4 years and phones every 3 years, or earlier if they fail."}, "cited_by_model": ["HR-203:v1.3:s6:c1", "OPS-105:v1.1:s6:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s6:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.658230185508728, "sections": ["HR-203#6"]}, {"id": "OPS-105:v1.1:s6:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.6161919832229614, "sections": ["OPS-105#6"]}, {"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s2:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.4926452040672302, "sections": ["HR-203#2"]}, {"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s5:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.4726420044898987, "sections": ["HR-203#5"]}, {"id": "HR-203:v1.3:s3:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.43903809785842896, "sections": ["HR-203#3"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 871, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 189, "reasoning_tokens": 79, "embedding_tokens": 10, "cost_usd": 0.00018180000000000003, "retrieval_ms": 158.9192000001276, "generation_ms": 2971.725299999889, "total_ms": 3130.6445000000167, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_3d5d05c95d51469b8eee3e2a31a698ec", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D023", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "The Change Advisory Board meets every Tuesday at 10:00. The supplied handbook passages do not provide a list of the rules you were given.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["OPS-102:v2.0:s4:c1"], "cited_text": {"OPS-102:v2.0:s4:c1": "The CAB meets every Tuesday at 10:00. It is chaired by the Head of IT Operations and includes the system owners and a representative from depot operations. A change that is not reviewed at CAB cannot go ahead, except as an emergency change."}, "cited_by_model": ["OPS-102:v2.0:s4:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s4:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.5097804665565491, "sections": ["OPS-102#4"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s2:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.4404554069042206, "sections": ["OPS-102#2"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s5:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.39764392375946045, "sections": ["OPS-102#5"]}, {"id": "OPS-102:v2.0:s7:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.34379222989082336, "sections": ["OPS-102#7"]}, {"id": "OPS-104:v2.2:s6:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.34302788972854614, "sections": ["OPS-104#6"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 952, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 227, "reasoning_tokens": 159, "embedding_tokens": 24, "cost_usd": 0.00020917999999999997, "retrieval_ms": 175.72930000005726, "generation_ms": 3290.450499999679, "total_ms": 3466.179799999736, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_83d313a2210e4cacb8dd0f6448ce5159", "warnings": []}
{"id": "D024", "status": "ok", "outcome": "answered", "answer": "The Service Desk is open on Saturdays, from 07:00 to 19:00.", "conflict_note": "", "citations": ["OPS-101:v3.0:s2:c1"], "cited_text": {"OPS-101:v3.0:s2:c1": "Report incidents to the IT Service Desk through the service portal or by phone on extension 4400. The Service Desk is staffed from 07:00 to 19:00, Monday to Saturday. Outside these hours, call the out-of-hours line on extension 4499, which pages the on-call engineer described in OPS-103.\nWhen you report an incident, give the site, the system affected, the time the problem started, how many people or vehicles are affected and any error message shown."}, "cited_by_model": ["OPS-101:v3.0:s2:c1"], "removed_citations": [], "retrieved": [{"id": "OPS-103:v1.4:s1:c1", "rank": 1, "score": 0.4226481318473816, "sections": ["OPS-103#1"]}, {"id": "OPS-101:v3.0:s2:c1", "rank": 2, "score": 0.4066303074359894, "sections": ["OPS-101#2"]}, {"id": "OPS-103:v1.4:s5:c1", "rank": 3, "score": 0.383364200592041, "sections": ["OPS-103#5"]}, {"id": "OPS-103:v1.4:s3:c1", "rank": 4, "score": 0.35373249650001526, "sections": ["OPS-103#3"]}, {"id": "OPS-103:v1.4:s2:c1", "rank": 5, "score": 0.34989213943481445, "sections": ["OPS-103#2"]}], "generation_skipped": false, "model": "gpt-6-luna", "input_tokens": 1007, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 82, "reasoning_tokens": 24, "embedding_tokens": 12, "cost_usd": 0.00014194, "retrieval_ms": 169.85730000033072, "generation_ms": 1525.5915999996432, "total_ms": 1695.448899999974, "provider_retries": 0, "provider_request_id": "req_cec0fa57caa043ea8f8f1e4ff553bbdb", "warnings": []}
